# Ask before packages / sudo

Do not run without explicit user OK: `sudo`, system package managers, or installs that change the env/lockfiles (`pip` / `uv` / `npm` / `idf.py add-dependency` / `cargo install`, etc.)—unless the user already asked for that exact action. Stop and ask instead.

Building with an already-configured ESP-IDF (`idf.py build` / `flash`) is fine without asking.
